%% Plan, subscription, entitlement, usage, and backend enforcement
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Operator as Platform admin
    participant API as Platform API
    participant Plans as Plan/subscription service
    participant DB as Control-plane PostgreSQL
    participant Usage as Usage service
    participant Feature as Tenant feature service
    participant Gate as EntitlementsService
    participant Tenant as Tenant PostgreSQL

    Operator->>API: Create/update plan catalog
    API->>Plans: Validate features, limits, interval, amount
    Plans->>DB: Persist plan and versioned entitlements

    Operator->>API: Assign subscription or trial to organization
    API->>Plans: Apply lifecycle status and effective plan
    Plans->>DB: Persist subscription and optional override

    Feature->>Gate: Evaluate organization + feature key + requested amount
    Gate->>DB: Load subscription, plan entitlement, active override
    DB-->>Gate: Status, enabled flag, and numeric limit
    opt Numeric entitlement
        Gate->>Usage: Read current period usage
        Usage->>DB: Load usage counter
        DB-->>Usage: Current value
    end

    alt Subscription and entitlement allow
        Gate-->>Feature: ALLOW with effective limit
        Feature->>Tenant: Apply tenant mutation or read
        Feature->>Usage: Record control-plane usage after durable fact
    else Missing, inactive, disabled, or over limit
        Gate-->>Feature: DENY with stable reason code
        Feature-->>API: Entitlement error
    end

    Operator->>API: Reconcile usage for organization
    API->>Usage: Compare tenant facts with recorded counters
    Usage->>Tenant: Read bounded authoritative tenant facts
    Usage->>DB: Correct control-plane counter and audit reconciliation

    Note over Feature,Gate: Frontend hiding is UX only; backend evaluation is enforcement.
    Note over DB,Tenant: Plans and usage counters live in the control plane; commerce facts remain tenant-owned and are only read for reconciliation.
